{"id": 3993566, "title": "CVE-2026-86414: leaking host credentials to HTTP proxy", "submitted": "2026-09-03", "source_url": "https://hackerone.com/reports/3993566", "excerpt": "Hi all,\n\nI've found that found that an untrusted HTTP proxy can trick libcurl into sending the *origin's* credentials (Basic password, or a Negotiate/Kerberos ticket) to the proxy itself, by answering the `CONNECT` tunnel request with `401 WWW-Authenticate` instead of the expected `407 Proxy-Authenticate`. Yes, the dreaded and well-known, \"malicious proxy\".\n\n## The bug\n\nBoth the H1 and H2/H3 CONNECT-response handlers decide whether a header applies to the proxy or the origin purely by status code:\n\n```c\n// lib/http_proxy.c:491-501 (Curl_http_proxy_inspect_tunnel_response, H2/H3)\nif(resp->status == 401) {\n    auth_reply = Curl_dynhds_cget(&resp->headers, \"WWW-Authenticate\");\n}\nelse if(resp->status == 407) {\n    auth_reply = Curl_dynhds_cget(&resp->headers, \"Proxy-Authenticate\");\n}\n\nif(auth_reply) {\n    ...\n    result = Curl_http_input_auth(data, resp->status == 407,\n                                  auth_reply->value);\n```\n\n```c\n// lib/cf-h1-proxy.c:396-406 (on_resp_header, H1)\nif((checkprefix(\"WWW-Authenticate:\", header) && (401 == k->httpcode)) ||\n   (checkprefix(\"Proxy-authenticate:\", header) && (407 == k->httpcode))) {\n\n    bool proxy = (k->httpcode == 407);\n    char *auth = Curl_copy_header_value(header);\n    ...\n    result = Curl_http_input_auth(data, proxy, auth);\n```\n\nBoth call `Curl_http_input_auth(data, proxy, ...)` with `proxy = (status == 407)`. For a `401` — which is what our malicious proxy returns — `proxy` is `false`, and `Curl_http_input_auth` updates `data->state.authhost`, the *origin's* auth state, not the proxy's:\n\n```c\n// lib/http.c:1067\nCURLcode Curl_http_input_auth(struct Curl_easy *data, bool proxy,\n                              const char *auth)\n{\n  ...\n  if(proxy) {\n    availp = &data->info.proxyauthavail;\n    authp = &data->state.authproxy;\n  }\n  else {\n    availp = &data->info.httpauthavail;\n    authp = &data->state.authhost;\n  }\n```\n\nThere is nothing anywhere in this call chain that knows \"we are still inside CONNECT, talking to the proxy, not the origin.\" A `401`/`WWW-Authenticate` at this point is entirely proxy-controlled input, but it is processed exactly as if it came from the real origin server.\n\nOnce `authhost.picked` is set this way (e.g. to `CURLAUTH_BASIC`), curl retries the `CONNECT` request, and `output_auth_headers()` — which decides what to attach to *any* request, including the CONNECT itself — has no check prevent", "excerpt_truncated": true, "final": "likely_valid", "final_label": "Confirmed by the code", "tone": "good", "explain": "The real code shows the flaw the report describes.", "confidence": 0.95, "judge_verdict": "likely_valid", "receipts_override": "", "policy_section": "", "grounding": {"verdict": "partially_grounded", "rev": "e26f6e408a80", "rev_source": "master on 2026-09-03", "counts": {"grounded": 35, "ungrounded_strong": 0, "ungrounded_medium": 1}, "problems": [{"check": "quote", "status": "ungrounded", "severity": "medium", "claim": "=== proxy log (exploit) ===", "evidence": "only 0/4 quoted lines appear anywhere in curl at e26f6e408a80"}]}, "summary": "A malicious HTTP proxy can trick libcurl into sending origin credentials (Basic password or Kerberos ticket) to itself by responding to a CONNECT tunnel request with 401 WWW-Authenticate instead of 407 Proxy-Authenticate, causing the credentials to be stored in the origin's auth state and leaked over the tunnel.", "claims": [{"id": "C1", "kind": "flaw", "text": "The CONNECT-response handlers decide whether a header applies to the proxy or the origin purely by status code (401 vs 407), without checking if the response is part of tunnel negotiation.", "status": "supported", "tone": "good", "reasoning": "Both CONNECT response handlers (H2/H3 in http_proxy.c and H1 in cf-h1-proxy.c) decide proxy vs origin scope solely by comparing the status code to 401 or 407. No additional check exists for whether the response is part of an ongoing CONNECT tunnel negotiation.", "citations": [{"file": "lib/http_proxy.c", "line": 492, "note": "Status code 401 selects WWW-Authenticate header and calls Curl_http_input_auth with proxy=false (resp->status == 407 is false)", "valid": true}, {"file": "lib/http_proxy.c", "line": 495, "note": "Status code 407 selects Proxy-Authenticate header and calls Curl_http_input_auth with proxy=true", "valid": true}, {"file": "lib/cf-h1-proxy.c", "line": 397, "note": "Condition checks for WWW-Authenticate with 401 or Proxy-Authenticate with 407", "valid": true}, {"file": "lib/cf-h1-proxy.c", "line": 400, "note": "proxy boolean set purely from (k->httpcode == 407)", "valid": true}]}, {"id": "C2", "kind": "location", "text": "The flaw occurs in the CONNECT tunnel response parsing code in lib/http_proxy.c and lib/cf-h1-proxy.c.", "status": "supported", "tone": "good", "reasoning": "The cited functions are the CONNECT tunnel response parsers for HTTP/2-3 and HTTP/1 respectively, and both contain the status-code-only logic.", "citations": [{"file": "lib/http_proxy.c", "line": 468, "note": "Function Curl_http_proxy_inspect_tunnel_response handles CONNECT tunnel responses for H2/H3", "valid": true}, {"file": "lib/cf-h1-proxy.c", "line": 388, "note": "Function on_resp_header handles CONNECT response headers for H1", "valid": true}]}, {"id": "C3", "kind": "trigger", "text": "A malicious proxy answers the CONNECT tunnel request with a 401 WWW-Authenticate header instead of the expected 407 Proxy-Authenticate.", "status": "supported", "tone": "good", "reasoning": "The code has explicit branches for handling 401 WWW-Authenticate during CONNECT response processing. A malicious proxy can trigger these branches by sending 401 instead of 407.", "citations": [{"file": "lib/http_proxy.c", "line": 492, "note": "Code path for 401 status exists and will be taken if proxy returns 401", "valid": true}, {"file": "lib/cf-h1-proxy.c", "line": 397, "note": "Code path for 401 with WWW-Authenticate header exists", "valid": true}]}, {"id": "C4", "kind": "impact", "text": "The origin's credentials (Basic password or Kerberos ticket) are stored in data->state.authhost and then sent over the cleartext proxy tunnel, leaking them to the proxy.", "status": "supported", "tone": "good", "reasoning": "When a 401 response is processed during CONNECT, proxy=false causes Curl_http_input_auth to update data->state.authhost (origin auth state). Later, output_auth_headers with proxy=false sends the origin's Basic credentials via Authorization header on the CONNECT retry, which goes to the proxy over the cleartext tunnel.", "citations": [{"file": "lib/http.c", "line": 1089, "note": "When proxy=false, authp points to data->state.authhost (origin auth state)", "valid": true}, {"file": "lib/http.c", "line": 1091, "note": "availp points to data->info.httpauthavail (origin auth avail)", "valid": true}, {"file": "lib/http.c", "line": 727, "note": "output_auth_headers Basic branch checks authstatus->picked == CURLAUTH_BASIC", "valid": true}, {"file": "lib/http.c", "line": 736, "note": "When proxy=false, uses data->state.creds (origin credentials) and emits Authorization header", "valid": true}, {"file": "lib/http.c", "line": 298, "note": "http_output_basic emits 'Authorization: Basic' when proxy=false, not 'Proxy-Authorization'", "valid": true}]}, {"id": "C5", "kind": "reproduction", "text": "The provided PoC script starts a malicious proxy that replies with 401 WWW-Authenticate during CONNECT, causing curl to send Authorization: Basic credentials over the tunnel.", "status": "supported", "tone": "good", "reasoning": "The PoC demonstrates the attack: a proxy that responds to CONNECT with 401 WWW-Authenticate causes curl to send Authorization: Basic with origin credentials over the tunnel. The control run (no 401) shows no credentials sent, confirming --anyauth works correctly without the attack.", "citations": [{"file": "reproduce.sh", "line": 1, "note": "PoC script starts malicious proxy that sends 401 WWW-Authenticate during CONNECT", "valid": false}, {"file": "reproduce.sh", "line": 50, "note": "curl invoked with -x (proxy), -p (proxytunnel), -u (credentials), --anyauth", "valid": false}, {"file": "reproduce.sh", "line": 30, "note": "Proxy sends 'HTTP/1.1 401 Unauthorized\\r\\nWWW-Authenticate: Basic realm=\"o\"\\r\\n' on first CONNECT", "valid": false}]}], "external_checks": [], "external_sources": [{"url": "https://docs.rs/hyper-util/latest/hyper_util/client/legacy/connect/proxy/struct.Tunnel.html", "title": "Tunnel in hyper_util::client::legacy::connect::proxy - Rust", "for": "The root cause is since commit 52ceab5e41 (2003-09-03, \"Re-arranged code to make the proxy-CONNECT loop able to do some of the authentication negotiations needed for NTLM, Digest etc.\"), the CONNECT-t"}], "key_reasons": ["The CONNECT tunnel response handlers in both http_proxy.c (H2/H3) and cf-h1-proxy.c (H1) use only the status code (401 vs 407) to decide whether an auth header applies to the proxy or the origin, with no check for whether the tunnel is still being negotiated.", "When a 401 WWW-Authenticate is received during CONNECT, Curl_http_input_auth is called with proxy=false, causing it to update data->state.authhost (origin auth state) instead of data->state.authproxy.", "On CONNECT retry, output_auth_headers with proxy=false emits 'Authorization: Basic' (not 'Proxy-Authorization') using data->state.creds (origin credentials), sending them over the cleartext tunnel to the proxy.", "The attack works even with --anyauth/CURLAUTH_ANY, which is documented to withhold credentials until challenged by the origin — but the proxy manufactures the challenge itself.", "The PoC reproduces the leak: the malicious proxy observes 'Authorization: Basic' on the tunneled request only when it injects the 401 during CONNECT."], "missing_info": [], "reply": "Thank you for the detailed report and reproducible PoC. The code confirms the flaw: during CONNECT tunnel negotiation, both H1 and H2/H3 response handlers treat a 401 WWW-Authenticate from the proxy as an origin challenge (proxy=false), poisoning authhost and causing origin credentials to be sent to the proxy on retry. This bypasses --anyauth's protection. We'll work on a fix that tracks tunnel-negotiation state and prevents origin auth state updates from proxy-controlled 401 responses during CONNECT.", "code": [{"name": "lib/http_proxy.c", "start": 466, "end": 526, "reason": "lines 491-501 cited by the report", "rows": [{"n": 466, "text": "}", "notes": []}, {"n": 467, "text": "", "notes": []}, {"n": 468, "text": "CURLcode Curl_http_proxy_inspect_tunnel_response(", "notes": ["C2: Function Curl_http_proxy_inspect_tunnel_response handles CONNECT tunnel responses for H2/H3"]}, {"n": 469, "text": "    struct Curl_cfilter *cf, struct Curl_easy *data,", "notes": []}, {"n": 470, "text": "    struct http_resp *resp, bool udp_tunnel,", "notes": []}, {"n": 471, "text": "    proxy_inspect_result *presult)", "notes": []}, {"n": 472, "text": "{", "notes": []}, {"n": 473, "text": "  struct dynhds_entry *capsule_protocol = NULL;", "notes": []}, {"n": 474, "text": "  struct dynhds_entry *auth_reply = NULL;", "notes": []}, {"n": 475, "text": "  size_t i, header_count;", "notes": []}, {"n": 476, "text": "  CURLcode result = CURLE_OK;", "notes": []}, {"n": 477, "text": "", "notes": []}, {"n": 478, "text": "  DEBUGASSERT(resp);", "notes": []}, {"n": 479, "text": "", "notes": []}, {"n": 480, "text": "  header_count = Curl_dynhds_count(&resp->headers);", "notes": []}, {"n": 481, "text": "  if(udp_tunnel)", "notes": []}, {"n": 482, "text": "    infof(data, \"CONNECT-UDP Response Status %d\", resp->status);", "notes": []}, {"n": 483, "text": "  else", "notes": []}, {"n": 484, "text": "    infof(data, \"CONNECT Response Status %d\", resp->status);", "notes": []}, {"n": 485, "text": "  infof(data, \"Response Headers (%zu total):\", header_count);", "notes": []}, {"n": 486, "text": "  for(i = 0; i < header_count; i++) {", "notes": []}, {"n": 487, "text": "    struct dynhds_entry *entry = Curl_dynhds_getn(&resp->headers, i);", "notes": []}, {"n": 488, "text": "    if(entry)", "notes": []}, {"n": 489, "text": "      infof(data, \"  %s: %s\", entry->name, entry->value);", "notes": []}, {"n": 490, "text": "  }", "notes": []}, {"n": 491, "text": "", "notes": []}, {"n": 492, "text": "  if(resp->status == 401) {", "notes": ["C1: Status code 401 selects WWW-Authenticate header and calls Curl_http_input_auth with proxy=false (resp->status == 407 is false)", "C3: Code path for 401 status exists and will be taken if proxy returns 401"]}, {"n": 493, "text": "    auth_reply = Curl_dynhds_cget(&resp->headers, \"WWW-Authenticate\");", "notes": []}, {"n": 494, "text": "  }", "notes": []}, {"n": 495, "text": "  else if(resp->status == 407) {", "notes": ["C1: Status code 407 selects Proxy-Authenticate header and calls Curl_http_input_auth with proxy=true"]}, {"n": 496, "text": "    auth_reply = Curl_dynhds_cget(&resp->headers, \"Proxy-Authenticate\");", "notes": []}, {"n": 497, "text": "  }", "notes": []}, {"n": 498, "text": "", "notes": []}, {"n": 499, "text": "  if(auth_reply) {", "notes": []}, {"n": 500, "text": "    CURL_TRC_CF(data, cf, \"[0] CONNECT%s: fwd auth header '%s'\",", "notes": []}, {"n": 501, "text": "                udp_tunnel ? \"-UDP\" : \"\", auth_reply->value);", "notes": []}, {"n": 502, "text": "    result = Curl_http_input_auth(data, resp->status == 407,", "notes": []}, {"n": 503, "text": "                                  auth_reply->value);", "notes": []}, {"n": 504, "text": "    if(result)", "notes": []}, {"n": 505, "text": "      return result;", "notes": []}, {"n": 506, "text": "    if(data->req.newurl) {", "notes": []}, {"n": 507, "text": "      curlx_safefree(data->req.newurl);", "notes": []}, {"n": 508, "text": "      *presult = PROXY_INSPECT_AUTH_RETRY;", "notes": []}, {"n": 509, "text": "      return CURLE_OK;", "notes": []}, {"n": 510, "text": "    }", "notes": []}, {"n": 511, "text": "  }", "notes": []}, {"n": 512, "text": "", "notes": []}, {"n": 513, "text": "  if(udp_tunnel) {", "notes": []}, {"n": 514, "text": "    if(resp->status / 100 == 2) {", "notes": []}, {"n": 515, "text": "      capsule_protocol = Curl_dynhds_cget(&resp->headers,", "notes": []}, {"n": 516, "text": "                                           \"capsule-protocol\");", "notes": []}, {"n": 517, "text": "      if(capsule_protocol) {", "notes": []}, {"n": 518, "text": "        if(!strncmp(capsule_protocol->value, \"?1\", 2) &&", "notes": []}, {"n": 519, "text": "           !capsule_protocol->value[2]) {", "notes": []}, {"n": 520, "text": "          infof(data, \"CONNECT-UDP tunnel established, response %d\",", "notes": []}, {"n": 521, "text": "                resp->status);", "notes": []}, {"n": 522, "text": "          *presult = PROXY_INSPECT_OK;", "notes": []}, {"n": 523, "text": "          return CURLE_OK;", "notes": []}, {"n": 524, "text": "        }", "notes": []}, {"n": 525, "text": "        failf(data, \"Failed to establish CONNECT-UDP tunnel, response %d, \"", "notes": []}, {"n": 526, "text": "              \"unsupported capsule-protocol value '%s'\",", "notes": []}], "cited": true}, {"name": "lib/cf-h1-proxy.c", "start": 371, "end": 431, "reason": "lines 396-406 cited by the report", "rows": [{"n": 371, "text": "                \"CONNECT-UDP Response --> Proxy-Connection: close\");", "notes": []}, {"n": 372, "text": "  }", "notes": []}, {"n": 373, "text": "  else if(!strncmp(header, \"HTTP/1.\", 7) &&", "notes": []}, {"n": 374, "text": "           ((header[7] == '0') || (header[7] == '1')) &&", "notes": []}, {"n": 375, "text": "           (header[8] == ' ') &&", "notes": []}, {"n": 376, "text": "           ISDIGIT(header[9]) && ISDIGIT(header[10]) && ISDIGIT(header[11]) &&", "notes": []}, {"n": 377, "text": "           !ISDIGIT(header[12])) {", "notes": []}, {"n": 378, "text": "    /* store the HTTP code from the proxy */", "notes": []}, {"n": 379, "text": "    data->info.httpproxycode = k->httpcode =", "notes": []}, {"n": 380, "text": "      ((header[9] - '0') * 100) +", "notes": []}, {"n": 381, "text": "      ((header[10] - '0') * 10) +", "notes": []}, {"n": 382, "text": "      (header[11] - '0');", "notes": []}, {"n": 383, "text": "    CURL_TRC_CF(data, cf, \"CONNECT-UDP Response --> %d\", k->httpcode);", "notes": []}, {"n": 384, "text": "  }", "notes": []}, {"n": 385, "text": "  return result;", "notes": []}, {"n": 386, "text": "}", "notes": []}, {"n": 387, "text": "", "notes": []}, {"n": 388, "text": "static CURLcode on_resp_header(struct Curl_cfilter *cf,", "notes": ["C2: Function on_resp_header handles CONNECT response headers for H1"]}, {"n": 389, "text": "                               struct Curl_easy *data,", "notes": []}, {"n": 390, "text": "                               struct h1_tunnel_state *ts,", "notes": []}, {"n": 391, "text": "                               const char *header)", "notes": []}, {"n": 392, "text": "{", "notes": []}, {"n": 393, "text": "  CURLcode result = CURLE_OK;", "notes": []}, {"n": 394, "text": "  struct SingleRequest *k = &data->req;", "notes": []}, {"n": 395, "text": "  (void)cf;", "notes": []}, {"n": 396, "text": "", "notes": []}, {"n": 397, "text": "  if((checkprefix(\"WWW-Authenticate:\", header) && (401 == k->httpcode)) ||", "notes": ["C1: Condition checks for WWW-Authenticate with 401 or Proxy-Authenticate with 407", "C3: Code path for 401 with WWW-Authenticate header exists"]}, {"n": 398, "text": "     (checkprefix(\"Proxy-authenticate:\", header) && (407 == k->httpcode))) {", "notes": []}, {"n": 399, "text": "", "notes": []}, {"n": 400, "text": "    bool proxy = (k->httpcode == 407);", "notes": ["C1: proxy boolean set purely from (k->httpcode == 407)"]}, {"n": 401, "text": "    char *auth = Curl_copy_header_